<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00970</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4b47b537-b6fd-4807-8b63-ba58c7868c7a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="d5a76d94-cf2d-48b0-bf90-ab0135ae6830" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00002">Evaluate \(\frac{140-20}{9-12}\) mentally.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00003">Correct! \(\frac{140-20}{9-12}=\frac{120}{-3}=-40\)</para><para id="para-00004">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.1.</para><para id="para-00005">The correct answer is -40.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="b7468d6e-f613-4347-80db-20b285dee5e0" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00006">Find the slope of the line that goes through the points \((1,-3)\) and \((2,4)\).:</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00007">Correct! \(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{4-(-3)}{2-1}=\frac{7}{1}=7\)</para><para id="para-00008">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.2.</para><para id="para-00009">The correct answer is 7.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e74a4667-56d7-487c-8a3c-d89ccc72b044" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00010">Write the equation of the line in slope-intercept form that goes through \((0,3)\) and has a slope of \(\frac14\) .</para>
      <para id="para-00011">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00012">\(y = -\frac{1}{4}x + 3\)</para><para id="para-00013">\(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\)</para><para id="para-00014">\(y = 3x + \frac{1}{4}\)</para><para id="para-00015">\(4x - y = -3 \)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00016">Correct! \(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\)</para><para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3.</para><para id="para-00018">The correct answer is \(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_78162944-7ce7-4725-9eeb-2dfeb4a0e30a" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00019">Write the equation of the line that passes through \((2,-1)\) and has a slope of \(-\frac{1}{2}\) in point-slope form.</para>
      <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00021">\(y = -\frac{1}{2}x -1\)</para><para id="para-00022">\(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\)</para><para id="para-00023">\(y = -\frac{1}{2}x\)</para><para id="para-00024">\(2x + y = 0\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00025">Correct! \(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\)</para><para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3.</para><para id="para-00027">The correct answer is \(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f90277af-e3c7-4ab4-9630-52aad43c5c02" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00028"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> equations that are correctly in standard form.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00029">Correct! \(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\)</para><para id="para-00030">\(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\) are in standard form because they are of the form \(Ax + By = C\).</para><para id="para-00031">They do not have any fractions or decimals and start with a positive coefficient.</para><para id="para-00032">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3.</para><para id="para-00033">The correct answer is \(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\)</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="d6d45287-acba-4ec5-be73-10739e3a7b6f" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00034">Write \(y = 4x - 2\) in standard form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00035">Correct! \(4x -y = 2\)</para><para id="para-00036">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y &amp;=&amp; 4x - 2\\ y - 4x &amp;=&amp; 4x - 4x - 2\\ -4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2 \\-1(-4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2) \\4x - y &amp;=&amp; 2\end{array}\)</para><para id="para-00037">Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4.</para><para id="para-00038">The correct answer is \(4x -y = 2\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_8c745b6e-b2ec-4fc2-92a8-44e56278d896" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00039">Write the equation \(y-4=-2(x-5)\) in slope-intercept form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00040">Correct! \(y=-2x+14\)</para><para id="para-00041">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-4&amp;=&amp;-2(x-5) \\ y-4&amp;=&amp;-2x+10\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+10+4\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+14\end{array}\)</para><para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4.</para><para id="para-00043">The correct answer is \(y=-2x+14\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="f9c71f6e-98ce-4efa-82bd-e267e9dd980e" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00044">Find the slope of the line between the points \((3,-1)\) and \((2,-4)\).</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00045">Correct! 3</para><para id="para-00046">\(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{-4-(-1)}{2-3}=\frac{-3}{-1}=3\)</para><para id="para-00047">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.2.</para><para id="para-00048">The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_8f1c5941-2186-4b07-b376-5ee300a9f4b6" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00049">Write the equation \(y-2=3(x+5)\) in standard form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00050">Correct! \(3x-y=-17\)</para><para id="para-00051">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-2&amp;=&amp;3(x+5)\\y-2&amp;=&amp;3x+15\\y-2-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x+15\\y-3x-2&amp;=&amp;15\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;15+2\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;17\\-1-3x+y&amp;=&amp;17\\3x-y&amp;=&amp;-17\end{array}\)</para><para id="para-00052">Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4.</para><para id="para-00053">The correct answer is \(3x-y=-17\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7fe6a5ff-1a71-478a-932d-5e5d7b0e7d4b" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00054">Evaluate \(\frac{36-48}{10-14}\) mentally.</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00055">Correct! 3</para><para id="para-00056">\(\frac{36-48}{10-14} =\frac{-12}{-4}=3\)</para><para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.1.</para><para id="para-00058">The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content></document>